ts need to share a scale."],[1540,"\\`xDomain\\` and \\`yDomain\\` pin the visible range. Use them to keep a fixed scale, or to keep several charts comparable."],[1531,"\\`xGridlines\\` and \\`yGridlines\\` add faint lines across the plot so it is easier to read a value back off an axis."],[1533,"\\`xLabels\\` and \\`yLabels\\` toggle the tick labels on each axis. Turn them off for sparklines or when the surrounding UI already names the values."],[1541,"\\`xNice\\` and \\`yNice\\` round the domain out to friendlier numbers (e.g. 0.2 to 1.0), so ticks land on values people expect."],[1544,"\\`xPaddingOuter\\` and \\`yPaddingOuter\\` add breathing room at the ends of a band or point scale so the first and last values are not pinned to the edges."],[1404,"\\`xTickFormat\\` and \\`yTickFormat\\` shape the axis labels - abbreviated dates on one axis, thousands separators on the other. The functions receive the raw accessor value, so they also cover currency, units, or percentages."],[1537,"\\`xTickFormat\\` and \\`yTickFormat\\` shape the axis labels - dates, currency, units, percentages - and the tooltip follows the same formatting."],[1534,"\\`xTickMarks\\` and \\`yTickMarks\\` draw the short lines at each tick value, which helps tie a label to its exact position on the axis."],[1532,"\\`xTitle\\` and \\`yTitle\\` label what each axis actually measures, e.g. \"Month\" and \"Temperature (°F)\"."],[1542,"\\`xZero\\` and \\`yZero\\` stretch the domain to include zero. Worth doing when the absolute size of the values matters, not just their movement."],[1189,"`--color-input-background-default`"],[1186,"`--color-input-background-selected`"],[1195,"`--color-input-text-default`"],[1196,"`--ux-1glcx6s`"],[1184,"`--ux-1m9ys0v`"],[1190,"`--ux-1nu8itt`"],[1193,"`--ux-1sbfig8`"],[1187,"`--ux-sywk25`"],[1199,"`--ux-zvaw3s`"],[436,"`[data-disabled]`"],[440,"`[data-focused]`"],[438,"`[data-invalid]`"],[176,"`@godaddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives."],[312,"`@godaddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives. Locale comes from a host `<I18nProvider>`. This version has no typed/segmented entry - selection is via the calendar."],[1599,"`<Box blockAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[1601,"`<Box inlineAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[1595,"`<Box orientation=\"horizontal\">`"],[1597,"`<Box orientation=\"vertical\">`"],[1602,"`<Flex alignItems=\"center\">`"],[1598,"`<Flex direction=\"column\" >`"],[1596,"`<Flex direction=\"row\" >`"],[1600,"`<Flex justifyContent=\"center\">`"],[1626,"`2xl` - 2x extra large spacing"],[463,"`acceptedFileTypes` is a best-effort filter for the OS picker — always validate file type and size again in your `onSelect` handler, since it can be bypassed."],[891,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[1063,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[287,"`aria-describedby` wires the `helperText` to the progressbar for screen readers"],[247,"`aria-disabled` for disabled checkboxes"],[892,"`aria-disabled` for disabled options"],[1064,"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"],[249,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[894,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1317,"`aria-label` (or `aria-labelledby`) is required on the group container"],[1065,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[366,"`aria-label=\"Close\"` on the built-in close button"],[286,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[843,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[248,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[893,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[284,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[841,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[840,"`aria-valuenow` reflects the current value"],[283,"`aria-valuenow` reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[842,